WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.367
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.834
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.534
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.567
During the first ballot in
today's House speakership vote,

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.100
Ohio congressman Jim Jordan

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.334
fell short of the 217 votes
necessary to become speaker.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.767
But Republicans are determined
to keep trying

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.868
until they finally get it wrong.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.801
During the first ballot in
today's House speakership vote,

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.133
several Republicans voted

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:27.033
for former New York
congressman Lee Zeldin,

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.934
which means they are
running out of options,

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:31.000
even alphabetically.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:31.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.634
"What about Ziggy Zyzax?

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:37.367
He's -- He's strong
on the border, right?"

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.033
Florida governor Ron DeSantis
over the weekend

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.934
announced that about
200 Floridians

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:44.367
were evacuated from Israel
and landed in Tampa,

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.567
marking the first time
in recorded history

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.267
that anyone was happy
to land in Tampa.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.667
"Well, maybe we'll
meet Tom Brady.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.868
What?

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.934
Retired?"

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.634
In a post today on Truth Social,

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:02.100
former president Trump said
that Ohio congressman Jim Jordan

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.234
will be a great House speaker
and added that he had

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.601
his "complete and total
endorsement."

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.100
"Good luck with that,"
said David Perdue, Kari Lake,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.767
Doug Mastriano,
Herschel Walker, Dr. Oz,

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.501
and that kid he forced
to mow his lawn.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.968
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.434
It's a long list.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:22.501
Justice Amy Coney Barrett
said in an interview yesterday

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:25.334
that the Supreme Court
should adopt an ethics code

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.701
and added, "All nine justices
are very committed

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.434
to the highest standards
of ethical conduct."

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:34.501
And when he read that interview,
Clarence Thomas laughed so hard,

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:37.300
he almost fell off
a billionaire's yacht.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.334
The drug manufacturer
Novo Nordisk announced yesterday

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.234
that it has acquired
a new hypertension drug

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.467
for $1.3 billion,

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.501
but they quickly
made that money back

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.033
after selling
five vials of insulin.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:55.934
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:59.400
I guess my question is, where
did we think the laugh was?

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:02.901
Like, as I'm saying it,
I'm like,

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.801
"Wait, this might not work."

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.200
Alright, well...

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.200
Got something pretty cool,
though,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.400
'cause you had to
suffer through that.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.567
Everybody look under your seat.
Vial of insulin.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.968
According to a new survey,

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:29.000
baby boomers said
their top source for new slang

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.434
is younger family members.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.434
Said your grandma,
"I crashed my whip

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.200
into the post office again."

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:38.601
According to the same survey,

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:41.834
the most popular new slang word
used in Florida is "sus."

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:45.567
Well, yeah.
Have you ever been there?

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:50.400
I'm surprised it's not also
the most popular baby name.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.734
"Yeah, we're calling him Sus.
We don't --

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.701
Doesn't look like either of us."

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.334 --> 00:03:00.467
Walmart has announced it will
offer the limited-edition

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:03.067
Van Leeuwen Kraft
Macaroni &amp; Cheese ice cream.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:06.434
It's a great way to make sure
your death is ruled a suicide.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.234
And finally --

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.634
You know would be good
with that?

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:16.634
Little vial of something.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.467
Not going to say what.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:21.667
And finally, Coca-Cola
and the makers of Absolut Vodka

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.634
announced yesterday
they're planning to release

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:26.634
a new ready-to-drink
vodka-Sprite cocktail,

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.100
because if you're mixing
vodka and Sprite,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.067
you're ready to drink.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:35.968
Yeah, I don't know, just two
liquids, one of them alcohol.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:37.367
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:38.467
We're off and running.

